| **All-positive total** | **1,718,669** | **196,083** | **1,522,586** | — | — |
| **Benchmark-eligible total (chr1–chrX)** | **1,716,832** | **196,083** | **1,520,749** | **1,520,120** | **629** |

The removed count for each chromosome equals the unique SVN-positive count for
that chromosome. Across the complete datasets, residual EVN/SVN overlap is zero,
and the clean EVN collection contains no duplicate cCRE IDs.

Each positive BED is stored as:

`chrom<chrom>/chrom<chrom>_GRCh38_ELS.bed`

Positive FASTAs and 1x synthetic-negative BED/FASTA pools have been generated for chr1-chr22 and chrX. Across the non-Y chromosomes, `genNullSeqs()` produced 1,520,120 synthetic negatives for 1,520,749 positives, a shortfall of 629 (0.041%). chrY is excluded from the benchmark and has no generated negative pool. Real-genomic background counts will be added after the active antinoise jobs finish. The old overlapping source pools and their historical negative counts remain under `../overlaps/chroms/`.
